Aerie-Purpose: Send chrome://filters to the Aerie Guard section of Settings and take the old filter lists page out of the browser.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc (HandleWebUI), chrome/browser/ui/webui/chrome_web_ui_configs.cc, chrome/browser/ui/webui/BUILD.gn, chrome/chrome_paks.gni, tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #103. HandleWebUI() rewrites chrome://filters to chrome://settings/aerieGuard, the
way it rewrites chrome://help, so the old address, the bookmarks that use it and the setup
page keep working. The rest of this patch removes what adblock/0009 added for the old
page: its WebUI config, its BUILD.gn label, its pak and its resource id range (10270 to
10279, which stays unused). The page's overlay directory is gone and its handler
is replaced by the one of adblock/0022.

--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
@@ -6599,4 +6599,9 @@
 constexpr char kLegacyOmniboxInternalsHost[] = "omnibox";
 
+// The former host of the filter lists page, chrome://filters. HandleWebUI()
+// rewrites it into the Aerie Guard section of Settings (issue #103).
+constexpr char kLegacyAerieFiltersHost[] = "filters";
+constexpr char kAerieGuardSettingsPath[] = "aerieGuard";
+
 bool IsDisabledInternalWebUI(const GURL& url) {
   if (!content::IsInternalWebUI(url)) {
@@ -7658,4 +7663,12 @@
   }
 
+  // Rewrite chrome://filters to chrome://settings/aerieGuard. The old page is
+  // gone; links, bookmarks and the setup page still use the address.
+  if (url->SchemeIs(content::kChromeUIScheme) &&
+      url->host() == kLegacyAerieFiltersHost) {
+    *url = ReplaceURLHostAndPath(*url, chrome::kChromeUISettingsHost,
+                                 kAerieGuardSettingsPath);
+  }
+
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC) || BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || \
     BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
